      "node_id": "kg_doc_20",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "New Richland is a city in Waseca County, Minnesota, United States. The city was founded in 1877. The population was 1,203 at the 2010 census. Located in rural south-central Minnesota, New Richland is a small town with a strong agricultural base. In 2013, the NRHEG High School Women's Basketball team won the State Tournament.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
